WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.890
You eat a meal full of
starch, protein and fat.

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.490
None of them can pass into
your blood as they are.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.730
Their molecules are far
too big to be absorbed.

4
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.710
Yet by the time your food
leaves the small intestine,

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.150
all three have been taken apart.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.390
So what are they broken down into?

7
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.870
In this mission, you'll see
how digestion turns large,

8
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.070
insoluble molecules into
small, soluble ones.

9
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.190
You'll meet three kinds of
digestive enzyme: amylase,

10
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.410
protease and lipase.

11
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.130
And you'll find out what bile does,

12
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.030
and why it isn't an enzyme at all.

13
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:38.830
Your mission: find out what
your food is broken into.
